From 5930e88f170b6b3e2b4718d9cdf364dcaf002fbf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 00:36:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] generic-parallel behaviours: shared data on several devices,
 shared code

- the data shared by all the integration points (`@SharedData`) are
  copied once per device with the CUDA and HIP backends (current device),
  and once per device and context with the SYCL backend, so that a
  process using several GPUs can share a library. The copy is identified
  by the function returning the data and shared by all the functions of a
  modelling hypothesis (one copy instead of one per generated function);
- the interfaces for behaviours and for models share the beginning and
  the end of the generated functions, the description of the library, the
  names of the generated files and library (given by the backend) and the
  selection of the backend by the interface options (backend factory,
  which lists the available backends if the backend is unknown);
- the host functions converting the statistics of a batch use the
  functions of `BatchData.h`: only the encoding used in device code is
  written in C++;
- the behaviour interface documentation gives the names of the symbols of
  the backend and of the version.

The comparison program integrates a batch on another device than the one
of the other tests, if any (`--other-device` option, SYCL only), for the
behaviour with shared data.
